WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.150
- It's the 25th anniversary
of Selena's passing.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.040
So what did you learn about
yourself playing Selena?

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.530
- Yeah, a lot.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.640
I also struggled with the
language like she did.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.440
She learned it as a young woman.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:18.260
And my grandparents came here from Mexico,

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.920
and I grew up in a
Spanish-speaking household,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.500
but my language was never perfect.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.060
And that was a small
insecurity of mine, you know?

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.580
It made me feel somehow like
less a part of my culture.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.040
And I realize now as an adult

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.540
that it doesn't matter
how far you are away

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.450
from your culture, there's
always time to reconnect,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.300
and it doesn't rob you
of anything that you are.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.330
- Yeah.
- So I was so proud

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.400
to play this woman, to
be filming in Mexico,

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.190
to be surrounded by my
culture, the language,

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.730
and be able to like get better
at it as she got better at it

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.490
during our show was really interesting.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.680
And it was my first opportunity
to really lead a show

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:54.010
and have that much responsibility.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.050
And I learned so much about business

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.980
and how I wanna go into
my next project, too,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.640
because she was such an inspiration

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.910
when it came to being strong

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.670
but also being incredibly graceful.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.030
- [Kelly] Yeah, being a great leader.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:06.863
- [Christian] Yeah.

00:01:06.863 --> 00:01:09.390
- I heard that even
Jennifer Lopez has mentioned

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.380
that she's excited for the series.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.700
So how does that make you feel?

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:13.830
'Cause I remember when she played Selena,

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.620
I was like, "Oh, my God, J.Lo."

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:17.680
I was a fan since she
was like a Fly Girl, so.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.130
- Yeah.
- Yeah, so I was very excited.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.660
But I think what's cool about it is,

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.077
and what she's probably excited about,

00:01:22.077 --> 00:01:23.660
is this is a whole new generation

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.150
that might not even know Selena.

00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.280
You know what I'm saying?
- Yeah.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.290
- And it's a shame.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:28.760
And it's really cool that you're doing it

00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:32.150
and paying tribute to this icon.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:34.570
Were you excited that
she was excited about it?

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:36.810
- Yeah, I didn't see that coming at all.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:37.780
And I-
- Yeah?

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:38.920
She's so sweet.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.650
- I hear that, yeah.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:42.330
- And I'm such a fan of hers

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.870
and grew up watching that movie.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.310
That movie was...

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.630
I know that movie backwards and forwards,

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.340
and she did such an
amazing job playing Selena,

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.180
which gives me a lot more pressure

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.900
'cause not only am I
stepping into Selena's shoes,

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:55.540
but I'm having to follow in
the footsteps of Jennifer.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.300
But I was so happy when I saw that.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.100
I saw it on social media
with everybody else.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.430
I didn't know that was coming.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:03.330
- That's cool.
- And it was

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.340
really heartwarming, yeah.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.980
- Yeah, that makes you feel good.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.580
It makes you feel confident
about what you're doing.

